{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":252190,"duration_api_ms":253778,"num_turns":1,"result":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** GNU Unix utilities have no formal specs accessible to implementers. This project derives formal specifications from C source, generates Go implementations from those specs using AI, and verifies parity via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract, specify, synthesize, verify). Shared `pkg/` libraries (testutils, sys, format, hashutil, sizeparse, encutil) support `cmd/` utility packages. Each `cmd/<name>/` has `main.go` + `<name>_test.go` with differential tests against `g<name>` reference binaries.\n\n**Implementation State:** Many utilities are implemented. Looking at `requirement_states`, the following SRDs have \"ready\" requirements: srd097-who (7), srd099-shred (11), srd100-chroot (6), srd101-install (11), srd102-tsort (7), srd103-pathchk (7), srd104-test (8), srd105-stty (11), srd106-df (18), srd107-dir (9), srd108-vdir (10), srd109-dircolors (14), srd110-pr (10), srd111-ptx (9), srd112-chronic (6), srd113-pee (5), srd114-vidir (6), srd004-ts (32).\n\n**Current Release Priority:** Release 11.1 (users/who/pinky) is the earliest incomplete release with ready requirements. users and pinky are implemented; only `who` remains (R2.1-R2.4, R3.1-R3.3). After 11.1, release 12.0 (shred/chroot/install) is next.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\n1. **Release 11.1 -- cmd/who:** R1.1-R1.4 were completed in task 5575. R2.1-R2.4 and R3.1-R3.3 remain ready. Two tasks complete this release.\n2. **Release 12.0 -- cmd/chroot:** Simplest of the three 12.0 utilities (6 requirements vs 11 each for shred/install). Two tasks complete chroot entirely. No contract needed -- cmd/ packages are main packages with no exports.\n\n## Weight Budget Check\n\nAssuming default weight=1 per requirement (weights not available in project_context):\n\n- Task 0: srd097 R2.1 (w=1) + R2.2 (w=1) + R2.3 (w=1) + R2.4 (w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 1: srd097 R3.1 (w=1) + R3.2 (w=1) + R3.3 (w=1) = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 2: srd100 R1.1 (w=1) + R1.2 (w=1) + R1.3 (w=1) = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 3: srd100 R2.1 (w=1) + R2.2 (w=1) + R2.3 (w=1) = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] Implement cmd/who extended session display (srd097 R2.1, R2.2, R2.3, R2.4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd097-who.yaml (R2.1-R2.4 requirement definitions)\n      - cmd/who/main.go (existing core implementation from R1.1-R1.4)\n      - cmd/who/who_test.go (existing differential tests)\n      - pkg/sys/ (system call abstractions for file metadata)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/who/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Extend who implementation with R2.1-R2.4 features\n      - path: cmd/who/who_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential test cases for R2.1-R2.4\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd097-who R2.1 per the SRD specification\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd097-who R2.2 per the SRD specification\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd097-who R2.3 per the SRD specification\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement srd097-who R2.4 per the SRD specification\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Use pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests to compare against gwho reference binary\n      - id: D2\n        text: Call exec.LookPath(\"gwho\") and t.Skip if reference binary not found\n      - id: D3\n        text: Set LC_ALL=C in test environment for deterministic output comparison\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: All R2.1-R2.4 behaviors from srd097-who.yaml are implemented in cmd/who/main.go\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go build ./cmd/who/ compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/who/ -count=1 passes\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: Differential tests against gwho pass for all R2.x features\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] Implement cmd/who error handling and differential tests (srd097 R3.1, R3.2, R3.3)\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd097-who.yaml (R3.1-R3.3 requirement definitions)\n      - cmd/who/main.go (existing implementation including R1.x and R2.x)\n      - cmd/who/who_test.go (existing differential tests)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/who/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add error handling and edge case support per R3.1-R3.3\n      - path: cmd/who/who_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential test cases for R3.1-R3.3 error scenarios\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd097-who R3.1 per the SRD specification\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd097-who R3.2 per the SRD specification\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd097-who R3.3 per the SRD specification\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Use pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests to compare against gwho reference binary\n      - id: D2\n        text: Call exec.LookPath(\"gwho\") and t.Skip if reference binary not found\n      - id: D3\n        text: Set LC_ALL=C in test environment for deterministic output comparison\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: All R3.1-R3.3 behaviors from srd097-who.yaml are implemented\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go build ./cmd/who/ compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/who/ -count=1 passes\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: Differential tests against gwho pass for all R3.x error cases\n\n- index: 2\n  title: \"[stitch] Implement cmd/chroot core functionality (srd100 R1.1, R1.2, R1.3)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd100-chroot.y